  "summary": "After Austin City Council ended APD's Flock license plate reader contract in June 2025, a KUT investigation found APD has continued to access Flock data through neighboring agencies including Round Rock and Sunset Valley police. Council members say the workaround violates the intent of city policy and the new TRUST Act surveillance ordinance, which they plan to tighten.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "A KUT investigation found the Austin Police Department accessed data from Flock Safety license plate readers maintained by neighboring law enforcement agencies within the last month.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "While APD no longer has the license plate reading cameras on city roads, it does have access to cameras maintained by at least two neighboring agencies: Round Rock and Sunset Valley police.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "Although use of other agencies [license plate reader] systems has not been specifically regulated by Council, we've made clear that we believe Flock systems pose an unacceptable risk to the liberty and privacy of our constituents",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "Siegel said the department's access to the license plate reader data would violate the TRUST Act",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    }
